## Original Content
U.S. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent told CNBC on Thursday that the proposed economic measures will likely negate the need for major U.S. military operations.

## Summary
The United States is preparing tough new economic sanctions against Iran, which Tehran has criticized as an example of 'extraterritorial sovereignty.' U.S. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent told CNBC that the proposed measures will likely negate the need for major U.S. military operations against Iran.

## Key Points
- Tough new U.S. sanctions targeting Iran are imminent
- Iran has condemned the sanctions as 'extraterritorial sovereignty'
- Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent believes the economic measures will likely make major U.S. military operations unnecessary
- Bessent made his comments in an interview with CNBC on Thursday


